  "rendered_excerpt": "OxfordAQA International Advanced Subsidiary Physics Revision Guide Exam board Oxford International AQA Examinations AQA Revision Guide Qualification family code: 9630 OxfordAQA International AS and A-level Physics OxfordAQA International Advanced Subsidiary Physics AS entry code 9631 Course identity AS OxfordAQA International Advanced Subsidiary Physics study guide Specification-led revision guide Specification / syllabus version Version 5.1 Target exam year 2027 01 Syllabus aligned 02 Topic based 03 Practice ready How to Study Study Order Stage 1 - Unit map: separate AS and A2 or modular units before mixing questions. Stage 2 - Build: turn each unit point into a short explanation, one application prompt, and one pitfall. Stage 3 - Test: practise by unit first, then combine units in mixed questions. Course Focus International AS Physics is a modular international qualification for study outside the United Kingdom. The AS stage uses Unit 1 (Mechanics, materials and atoms) and Unit 2 (Electricity, waves and particles). Each AS unit is a two-hour, 80-mark written paper worth 50% of AS and 20% of the full International A-level. The Version 5.1 specification assesses practical knowledge through written papers rather than a separate practical examination. Guide Setup Subject request: International AS Physics 9631 Term support: English with zh-CN glossary Illustrations: custom illustration model: gpt-image-2 Writing style: Formal Professional Term Glossary The handbook body stays in English for the exam. This table gives Simplified Chinese support for key terms. Simplified Chinese English exam term Exam use 位移 Displacement A vector change in position. 速率 Speed Distance travelled per unit time. 速度 Velocity Rate of change of displacement. 加速度 Acceleration Rate of change of velocity. 合力 Resultant force The single force with the same effect as all forces combined. 力矩 Moment Force multiplied by perpendicular distance from a pivot. 力偶 Couple Two equal opposite parallel forces with a turning effect. 质心 Centre of mass The point at which the mass of a body may be considered concentrated. 密度 Density Mass per unit volume. 应力 Stress Force per unit cross-sectional area. 应变 Strain Extension divided by original length. 杨氏模量 Young modulus Tensile stress divided by tensile strain in the elastic region. 弹性限度 Elastic limit The greatest load or stress for which deformation is reversible. 动量 Momentum Mass multiplied by velocity. 冲量 Impulse Force multiplied by time, equal to change in momentum. 做功 Work done Energy transferred by a force moving through a distance. 功率 Power Rate of energy transfer. 效率 Efficiency Useful output energy or power divided by input energy or power. 电荷 Charge A property responsible for electrical interactions. 电流 Current Rate of flow of charge. 电势差 Potential difference Energy transferred per unit charge. 电阻 Resistance Potential difference divided by current. 电阻率 Resistivity A material property linking resistance to length and cross-sectional area. 电动势 Electromotive force (emf) Energy supplied by a source per unit charge. 内电阻 Internal resistance Resistance inside a source that causes lost volts. 热敏电阻 Thermistor A temperature-dependent resistor. 振动 Oscillation Repeated motion about an equilibrium position. 振幅 Amplitude Maximum displacement from equilibrium. 周期 Period Time for one complete cycle. 频率 Frequency Number of complete cycles per unit time. 阻尼 Damping Energy loss that reduces oscillation amplitude. 共振 Resonance Large response when driving frequency is close to natural frequency. 波长 Wavelength Distance between adjacent points in phase. 相位差 Phase difference Fraction of a cycle separating two oscillations. 偏振 Polarisation Restriction of transverse vibration to one direction. 叠加 Superposition Resultant displacement when waves overlap. 驻波 Stationary wave A pattern of nodes and antinodes formed by opposing waves. 节点 Node A point of zero displacement in a stationary wave. 腹部 Antinode A point of maximum displacement in a stationary w"
}
